---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy: Helix Tech"
  description="What helixtech.app keeps about its visitors, which is next to nothing, and where the contact form sends what you write."
  image="/og/privacy.png"
>
  <article class="wrap privacy">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Privacy</p>
    <h1 data-reveal>Nothing to track.</h1>
    <p class="lede" data-reveal>
      This site is a set of static pages. It sets no cookies, runs no analytics and loads nothing from anyone else: no
      scripts, no fonts, no images, no trackers.
    </p>

    <div class="sections">
      <section data-reveal>
        <h2>What the site keeps</h2>
        <p>
          If you pick a theme with the switch in the header, that choice is kept in your own browser’s storage so the
          page opens the same way next time. It never leaves your browser, and clearing site data removes it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The server writes the usual access log: the requested page, the time, your IP address and your browser’s
          name. It exists to spot and block abuse, and is read by nothing else.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-reveal>
        <h2>The contact form</h2>
        <p>
          The <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> is delivered by <a href="https://web3forms.com">Web3Forms</a>.
          What you type (your name, email address, subject and message) goes to them and on to Helix Tech by email,
          and a copy stays in their dashboard. Their handling of it is set out in the{' '}
          <a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy">Web3Forms privacy policy</a>. Your message is used to reply to you
          and for nothing else. If you would rather not use the form, email works the same.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-reveal>
        <h2>Links elsewhere</h2>
        <p>
          The tools, their issues and their releases live on GitHub. Once you follow a link there, GitHub’s own{' '}
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">privacy statement</a>
          {' '}applies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-reveal>
        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>Ask through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
        <p class="updated">Last updated 30 October 2026.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <p data-reveal>
      <a class="button" href="/">Back to the home page <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem) clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
  }
  .lede {
    max-width: 52ch;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }
  .sections {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  }
  section {
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
</style>
